<!--
    kuna castsign (P9, sub-stage cast-policy; option castsign on|off).

    Source: the 2026-09-23 cast census.  `signedness auto` re-declares a
    register local signed when every signedness-sensitive reader of it is
    signed, but it skips every high mapped onto a Symbol, and a stack local is
    mapped onto its frame Symbol; it also vetoes a variable used as a pointer
    index.  So a frame-resident index that the program only compares signed
    stays `uint8` and every comparison carries `(int8)v1`.

    gcc -O0 -fno-pie -fno-stack-protector, linked at 0x1000 (the bytes below
    are .text), with ulen and fill declared below:

      ulen(s)          declared below: extern uint8 ulen(char *s)
      fill(p)          declared below: extern void fill(uint8 *p)
      trim_right(s)    { long i = ulen(s) - 1;
                         while (i >= 0 && s[i] == ' ') { s[i] = 0; i -= 1; }
                         return i * 10 + 3; }
      halved(s)        { unsigned long n = ulen(s) - 2;
                         if ((long)n < 0) return -1; return (long)(n >> 1); }
      through_ptr()    { unsigned long n; fill(&n);
                         if ((long)n < 0) return -3; return (long)n; }

    Pass 1 (option castsign off) reproduces the defect: trim_right's stack
    index is declared uint8 and its signed comparison casts it back (#1, #2).
    Pass 2 (option castsign on) declares it int8 and the cast, now a no-op, is
    dropped (#3, #4); the `a0[v1]` pointer index is signedness-neutral at
    pointer width.  Both passes keep halved's register value unsigned, since it
    is shifted right logically (#5), and through_ptr's stack value unsigned,
    since its address is passed as a uint8 * (#6).  Pass 3 (option castsign
    still on) maps trim_right's slot as `uint8 idx`, which locks its type the
    way a DWARF local or a type assertion does: the declaration and its cast
    stay (#7, #8).
-->
